WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.656
If something happened to both parents,

2
00:00:03.656 --> 00:00:07.110
who would raise your children?

3
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:09.073
If you haven't said,

4
00:00:09.073 --> 00:00:10.640
a court decides.

5
00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:14.494
It looks at what's in the child's best interests,

6
00:00:14.494 --> 00:00:17.600
often starting with relatives.

7
00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.469
Courts usually give weight to the guardian

8
00:00:21.469 --> 00:00:23.677
you name in your will,

9
00:00:23.677 --> 00:00:27.100
though they still review it.

10
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:28.919
Name a backup.

11
00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:32.772
Pick someone whose values and home you trust,

12
00:00:32.772 --> 00:00:36.100
not just a favorite relative.

13
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.471
Separate from guardian of the person,

14
00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:42.256
you can set up money management,

15
00:00:42.256 --> 00:00:44.235
often through a trust,

16
00:00:44.235 --> 00:00:47.792
so the guardian doesn't have to ask a court

17
00:00:47.792 --> 00:00:49.600
for funds.

18
00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:55.038
Our guide has questions to talk over with your partner.

19
00:00:55.038 --> 00:00:57.100
Start there.
